cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Iris in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Iris: evaluation of AI agent output for quality, safety and cost"
abstract: >-
  Iris is an open-source MCP server that evaluates AI agent output for
  quality, safety and cost. Send Iris a run and ask for a verdict: it judges
  the run with deterministic built-in rules (PII, prompt injection,
  hallucination markers, cost, and the agent's own tool calls) and an optional
  model judge on your own key with a hard per-evaluation cost cap, and answers
  pass, fail, or not checked when a required check could not run. Runs are
  stored in SQLite on your own machine. The precision and recall of every
  built-in rule are measured on a labelled corpus in the repository and
  published with confidence intervals.
authors:
  - given-names: Ian
    family-names: Parent
version: "0.21.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/iris-eval/mcp-server"
repository-artifact: "https://www.npmjs.com/package/@iris-eval/mcp-server"
url: "https://iris-eval.com"
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp-server
  - ai-agents
  - agent-evaluation
  - llm-evaluation
  - llm-as-judge
  - pii-detection
  - prompt-injection
  - opentelemetry
